# MT7925 WiFi Authentication Failures - 2026-01-12 19:59

## System Info
- Kernel: 6.18.4-2-cachyos-wifi-fix
- Driver: mt7925e
- ASIC: 79250000
- Firmware: 20251015213023

## Symptoms
- WiFi connection dropped
- Multiple authentication failures when trying to reconnect
- Had to reboot to restore connectivity

## Key Errors

### Authentication request failed
```
Jan 12 19:59:51 wlan0: SME: Authentication request to the driver failed
```

### Deauthentication - Class 2 frame from non-authenticated station
```
Jan 12 19:59:55 wlan0: deauthenticated from de:b3:70:f8:89:51 while associating (Reason: 6=CLASS2_FRAME_FROM_NONAUTH_STA)
```

### Deauthentication - 4-way handshake timeout
```
Jan 12 19:59:59 wlan0: deauthenticated from de:b3:70:f8:9e:7d (Reason: 15=4WAY_HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT)
Jan 12 20:00:12 wlan0: deauthenticated from de:b3:70:f8:89:51 (Reason: 15=4WAY_HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT)
```

## Timeline
1. 19:59:51 - Tried to authenticate with AP on 6135 MHz (WiFi 6E)
2. 19:59:51 - "Authentication request to the driver failed"
3. 19:59:54 - Tried different AP on 5280 MHz
4. 19:59:54 - AP rejected association temporarily (comeback duration 1024ms)
5. 19:59:55 - Deauth: CLASS2_FRAME_FROM_NONAUTH_STA
6. 19:59:59 - Deauth: 4WAY_HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT
7. 20:00:12 - More 4WAY_HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT failures
8. 20:01:14 - System rebooted

## Analysis
The driver appears to have gotten into a bad state where it couldn't complete authentication. The "Authentication request to the driver failed" suggests an internal driver issue, not an AP-side problem.

This is likely related to:
- MLO (Multi-Link Operation) state corruption
- WiFi 6E band switching issues
- Driver state machine getting stuck

## Related Patches
The kernel being built should include patches for:
- NULL pointer dereference fixes in vif/link handling
- Mutex protection for concurrent operations
- Better error handling in authentication paths
